task_brief: {"domain": "elective spinal fusion surgeries, Cedars-Sinai Medical Center, Los Angeles, 2013-2025", "prediction_task": "binary", "target_column": "discharge_Non_Home", "positive_class": 1, "expected_positive_rate": 0.273, "selection_metric": "average_precision", "num_classes": 2, "group_column": null, "notes": "Predict the adverse outcome of discharge to a non-home facility (SNF / rehab / another hospital) after elective spinal fusion surgery. Dataset: 7108 surgeries x 126 feature columns + the target. Each row is a unique surgery, so no group-aware splitting is required. Target `discharge_Non_Home` is derived from the raw discharge disposition (0 = Home; 1 = any SNF, rehab, or other-hospital transfer); every other discharge-related column has been dropped, so there is no residual outcome leakage. FEATURE FAMILIES: continuous AGE, BMI, SBP, PAIN_SCORE; comorbidities `pmh_*` (binary); medications `med_*` (binary); procedure characteristics `pn_*` (binary, e.g. cervical/thoracic/lumbar level, revision); lab values `lab_*` (continuous). Demographic and social-history categoricals are ALREADY one-hot encoded \u2014 `gender_*`, `age_*` bands, `race_*`, `insurance_*`, `ms_*` (marital status), `tobacco_use_*`, `alcohol_use_*`, `drug_use_*`, `pain_score_*` \u2014 so they do NOT need re-encoding; `_nan`/`_unknown` dummies already carry the missing categories. Impute detected missing values with thetrain-fit only (mode for binary/categorical, mean or median for continuous). A per-column data dictionary is available via get_data_dictionary."}

